{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"stable-diminutive-thrasher","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\n`main` is red at 2e85d8558a4: `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py::test_no_src_call_decodes_child_output_with_the_locale_codec` flags `src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py:61`, a `subprocess.run(..., text=True)` with no `encoding=`. Every change based on current main fails `Verified` on it.\n\n## Cause\n\nTwo changes raced. d5f10d1d2c8 (golden-busied-nag) added the call and passed CI before 37d83e8f308 (dogtired-blank-fieldmouse) added the tree-wide guard that rejects text-mode child output decoded with the locale codec. Each passed CI on its own base; their combination on main does not. Without an explicit encoding, `git show` output (the committed `rebar.toml`) is decoded with the locale code page on Windows, so a non-ASCII byte in that file would fail or mis-decode.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `encoding=\"utf-8\"` to that `subprocess.run` call, matching the guard's contract and the rest of `src/rebar`. No other behaviour changes; no new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py`\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py` passes on the change (it fails on 2e85d8558a4).\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py` passes on the change.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the change.\n- [ ] The Gerrit change merges with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.","id":"1290-60d3-8e93-44c8","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Op-cert gate config decodes git output with the locale codec"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795250996032018001,"uuid":"daffaceb-0b7d-4769-86bf-329510d98bad"}